    <string name="cert_manual_title">Manual install</string>
    <string name="cert_manual_steps">1. Tap “Install certificate” above — the system dialog should appear.\n2. If nothing appears, tap “Open system certificate settings”, then Security → Encryption &amp; credentials → Install a certificate → CA certificate.\n3. Pick the hudsucker.cer you exported to Downloads.\n4. Confirm the “network may be monitored” warning.</string>
    <string name="cert_warning_title">About the Android 7+ restriction</string>
    <string name="cert_warning_body">A user-installed CA is only honoured by apps that opt into user certificates. Browsers (including the built-in one here) work fine; some game clients ignore user CAs, in which case use the built-in browser, or move the certificate into the system store on a rooted device.</string>
    <string name="cert_install_unsupported">This ROM exposes no certificate installer — please install manually.</string>

